title: Kapp Flees
subtitle: The putsch collapses. Legien wants a workers' government.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: crisis_kapp = 1 and crisis_time = 2 and kapp_decided = 0 and (strike_count >= 3 or e20_kapp_army = 1)
max-visits: 1
priority: 5
on-arrival: {!
Q.kapp_decided = 1;
// how much weight the workers have in Berlin now: the strike, our voice in it, our demands
Q.e20_wg_score = Q.strike_count * 6 + Q.e20_kapp_voice * 8 + Q.e20_kapp_demands * 5 + (Q.uspd_relation - 45) / 2 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 11);
RG.news('Kapp flees to Sweden: the putsch collapses', 3);
!}

= Kapp Flees

On 17 March Kapp resigned and fled to Sweden. The next day the Ehrhardt Brigade marched out of Berlin, and at the Brandenburg Gate it fired into the crowd that jeered it.

The strike goes on. Carl Legien, the most cautious union leader in Germany, demands Noske's resignation, the punishment of the putschists and the socialisation of the mines. Then he goes further: let the SPD, the USPD and the unions form a **workers' government**, without the bourgeois parties. The USPD leaders are suspicious, and they ask what the communists will do.

- @loyal: Promise a loyal opposition to a workers' government.
- @support: Urge the USPD to accept, and offer to support the government.
- @fraud: Denounce the offer as a trick to end the strike.

@loyal
subtitle: We will not overthrow a socialist government by force while it lets the workers organise. Lenin will approve.
on-arrival: {!
Q.wg_stance = 1;
Q.kapp_outcome = Q.e20_wg_score >= 68 ? 3 : 1;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
RG.ecci('lenin', 8);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -4);
!}

We publish the statement on 23 March. [? if kapp_outcome = 3 : It is enough. Crispien and Däumig go to the Chancellery with Legien. ?][? if kapp_outcome = 1 : It is not enough. The USPD leaders will not sit with the party of Noske, and the old coalition returns under Hermann Müller. ?]

- @ruhr: Continue...

@support
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The best chance of a workers' government. The Left will never forgive it.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids supporting a government of social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.wg_stance = 2;
Q.kapp_outcome = Q.e20_wg_score + 9 >= 68 ? 3 : 1;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 10;
Q.lean_unionist += 3;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -6);
!}

[? if kapp_outcome = 3 : The Independents cannot refuse what even the communists demand. Legien becomes Chancellor of a government of the SPD, the USPD and the unions. ?][? if kapp_outcome = 1 : The USPD leaders refuse all the same. The old coalition returns under Hermann Müller. ?]

- @ruhr: Continue...

@fraud
subtitle: No illusions, and no end to the strike. The USPD leaders will be glad of the excuse.
on-arrival: {!
Q.wg_stance = 3;
Q.kapp_outcome = 1;
Q.militancy += 5;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
RG.ecci('bukharin', 5);
RG.ecci('lenin', -4);
!}

The old coalition returns under Hermann Müller, and the unions call off the strike.

- @ruhr: Continue...

@ruhr
title: The Red Army of the Ruhr
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.crisis_kapp = 0;
Q.crisis_ruhr = 1;
Q.crisis_name = 'The Ruhr Red Army';
Q.crisis_goal = 'Hold the coalfield, and decide whether to sign at Bielefeld or fight on.';
Q.crisis_momentum_label = 0;
Q.freikorps_strength -= 60;
Q.stability -= 5;
if (Q.kapp_outcome == 3) {
    Q.government_name = 'Workers\' government (SPD, USPD, unions)';
    Q.chancellor = 'Carl Legien';
    Q.spd_in_government = 1;
    Q.uspd_in_government = 1;
    Q.zentrum_in_government = 0;
    Q.ddp_in_government = 0;
    Q.dvp_in_government = 0;
    Q.worker_support += 6;
} else if (Q.kapp_outcome != 2) {
    Q.government_name = 'Müller cabinet (SPD, Centre, DDP)';
    Q.chancellor = 'Hermann Müller';
    Q.spd_in_government = 1;
    Q.zentrum_in_government = 1;
    Q.ddp_in_government = 1;
    Q.army_loyalty += 10;
}
// the Red Army: men and towns, against Watter's troops gathering at Münster
Q.e20_ruhr_towns = 12 + (Q.e19_ruhr_cells ? 2 : 0);
Q.e20_ruhr_men = 40 + (Q.kapp_armed ? 10 : 0) + (Q.e19_ruhr_cells ? 5 : 0) + Q.e20_ruhr_extra;
Q.e20_ruhr_watter = Q.kapp_outcome == 3 ? 12 : 20;
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    if (d != 'ruhr') { RG.endStrike(d, Q.kapp_outcome == 3 ? 'won' : 'quiet'); }
}
RG.district('ruhr', {guards: 30, loyalty: 6, members: 0.2});
Q.crisis_line_1 = 'Towns held: ' + Q.e20_ruhr_towns;
Q.crisis_line_2 = 'Red Army: ' + Q.e20_ruhr_men + ',000 men';
Q.crisis_line_3 = 'Watter\'s troops at Münster: ' + Q.e20_ruhr_watter + ',000';
if (Q.kapp_outcome == 3) { RG.news('Legien forms a workers\' government', 3); }
else if (Q.kapp_outcome == 1) { RG.news('Unions call off the strike; Müller forms a cabinet', 3); }
RG.news('Red Army of the Ruhr holds the coalfield from the Rhine to Hamm', 3);
!}

= The Red Army of the Ruhr

[? if kapp_outcome != 2 : The strike is over in Berlin. ?][? if kapp_outcome = 2 : Berlin belongs to the generals. ?] In the Ruhr it has become a war. Armed miners and steelworkers have driven the Reichswehr and the Freikorps out of Dortmund, Essen, Bochum and Duisburg. They call themselves the Red Army. Their front runs along the Lippe, and they are besieging the fortress of Wesel.

Two central councils claim to lead them: one in Hagen, run by the USPD, and one in Essen, where our comrades and the syndicalists are strong. [? if kapp_outcome = 3 : The workers' government has ordered General von Watter not to cross the Lippe. ?][? if kapp_outcome = 1 : At Münster General von Watter is gathering the same Freikorps that marched with Kapp, and Berlin is letting him. ?]
